  "notes": "Complete Giurgeni – Vadu Oii crossing: five haunched main river spans on four battered cutwater piers, long graded smaller-pier approaches, full four-lane roadway, concrete verge walks, W guardrails and shared expanded-metal outer fencing, paired curved two-height streetlight arms and distinct bank abutments. The full1499.943m mapped envelope controls placement; the720m river core is not substituted for the whole crossing. Ordinary-picture exterior approximation, not a surveyed engineering model. The river panorama and road photograph control the five-span haunched form, broad four-lane deck, open metal fencing and curved paired lamps. One unrelated stock picture showing a railway/truss crossing is excluded. The retained1499.943m envelope includes approach viaducts; reported1464m length is a separate scope measure. Concealed structure, support spacing, haunch depths, profile elevations, bearings and below-ground foundations are photo/map-guided approximations. No copied mesh, private photo texture, vehicles or readable signs. Native terrain is coarse; physical-device timing remains unmeasured. Native water uses the original standard terrain and actual polygon/river-ribbon renderer; no favorable flat water plane or terrain flattening is authored. The two mapped farm tracks are retained unchanged and receive no authored approach profiles. Six width-distributed track probes pass at every LOD with no horizontal obstruction: minimum sampled headroom4.819m across all tiers and5.922m close-up. These are visualization fit checks, not engineering clearance certification. Native automatic fallback and coarse terrain remain unchanged when the model is absent. Native default-width approach roads are preserved; the end verge walks are not claimed to continue into mapped sidewalks.",
